    "body": "P2PK proof witness is encoded 3 times, corrupting the CBOR token.\n\n1. KeyRingService.ts:97 - JSON.stringify when signing (1st)\n2. ProofRepository.ts:60 - JSON.stringify on DB save (2nd)\n3. @cashu/cashu-ts - JSON.stringify on token encodeing (3rrd)\n\nThose Double stringify from coco impacted \nAfter token decoding, witness.signaturs is undefined\nP2PK signature verification always fails\nTokens cannot be shared with other wallets (no one can decode properly cuz still Stringify'd after decode)\n\nFiles to Fix (5 total)\n- packages/core/services/KeyRingService.ts:97\n- packages/sqlite3/src/repositories/ProofRepository.ts:60\n- packages/sqlite-bun/src/repositories/ProofRepository.ts:60\n- packages/expo-sqlite/src/repositories/ProofRepository.ts:60\n- packages/indexeddb/src/repositories/ProofRepository.ts:48\n\nFix\n- KeyRingService: return witness as object (remove JSON.stringify)\n- Repositories: Check if string before encoding (prevent double-encoding)\n\nSmall fix (~2 days), but I want to confirm the bug behavior first.",
